# Car exterior frames

Applies when B-roll / subject is a **car** (Porsche, Ferrari, GT3, coupe, etc.). Skip for yachts, watches, houses.

## When vetting frames

Every kept clip and frame is the **outside** of the car. Drop cabin, cockpit, steering wheel, dashboard, seats, interior POV, and windshield-from-inside. Do not keep a clip that is mostly interior. Frame rate + resolution: see `broll-clip-quality.mdc` (any readable fps, 4K optional).

```
# ❌ BAD — inside
dashboard, wheel in lap, leather seats, cabin night-drive POV

# ✅ GOOD — outside
full body in driveway, three-quarter street, side profile rolling, front 3/4 night
```

Wheel / taillight / badge close-ups are OK **after** the opener. Never as the start. Never instead of an exterior.

## Opener (required)

Car videos **start** on a full view of the car. Hold that exterior at least **5 seconds** before cutting to detail, cabin, or another shot.

Full view = most of the body visible (front, three-quarter, or side). Not rear-only. Not taillights. Not a person with a car in the background.

This overrides DrivenVisuals 1–2s / fast-beat opener **for cars**.

When reviewing the output mp4, check **0s, ~2.5s, and 5s**. All three must show the car from outside. The start must be a wide/full body.

If first 5s is cabin, host, house, or a cropped piece of the car — gate failed. Do not ship. Pick another clip or re-cut.
